From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: omit inactive clients from cached association stats

The associated-device monitor correctly marks a cached station inactive when
the HAL no longer reports it on that VAP.  Its cached-provider copy path then
ignored cli_Active and exported every historical row anyway.  EasyMesh used
that provider path, so an intra-agent band roam could leave the client on the
old BSSID indefinitely even though the station was present only on the new
BSSID in the kernel.

Only copy active rows and report the number actually copied.  The allocation
may remain sized to the cache as a harmless upper bound.  This makes the
cached provider honor the same live-associated-device contract as the direct
collector path.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/stats/wifi_stats_assoc_client.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/stats/wifi_stats_assoc_client.c b/source/stats/wifi_stats_assoc_client.c
--- a/source/stats/wifi_stats_assoc_client.c
+++ b/source/stats/wifi_stats_assoc_client.c
@@ -695,13 +695,15 @@ int copy_assoc_client_stats_from_cache(wifi_mon_provider_element_t *p_elem, void
         to_sta_key(temp_sta->sta_mac, sta_key);
         wifi_util_dbg_print(WIFI_MON, "%s:%d vap_index %d count : %d sta_key : %s\n",
                 __func__, __LINE__, args->vap_index, count, sta_key);
-        memcpy(&sta[count], temp_sta, sizeof(sta_data_t));
-        count++;
+        if (temp_sta->dev_stats.cli_Active == true) {
+            memcpy(&sta[count], temp_sta, sizeof(sta_data_t));
+            count++;
+        }
         temp_sta = hash_map_get_next(sta_map, temp_sta);
     }
 
     *stats = sta;
-    *stat_array_size = sta_count;
+    *stat_array_size = count;
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&mon_cache->data_lock);
     return RETURN_OK;
 }
